poll(): revents translated for EVERY entry, not the first ret.

ret is how many entries are ready, not which: with a ready entry after
an idle one, the ready entry's revents went back untranslated. Only the
bits m68k moves differ (POLLWRNORM, POLLWRBAND), so it showed only to a
program asking for those. ppoll (the m68k backend's events.c) maps every
entry already.

--- a/libos/linux/poll.c	2026-10-01 17:21:43.585293378 -0600
+++ b/libos/linux/poll.c	2026-10-01 17:21:43.622019818 -0600
@@ -133,8 +133,9 @@
     for (n = 0; n < nfds; n++)
         fds[n].events = linux_to_picolibc(fds[n].events);
 
-    if (ret > 0) {
-        for (n = 0; n < (nfds_t)ret; n++)
+    /* Every entry: ret is how many are READY, not which. */
+    if (ret >= 0) {
+        for (n = 0; n < nfds; n++)
             fds[n].revents = linux_to_picolibc(fds[n].revents);
     }
     return ret;
